<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/10th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Riade</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">933</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Riade was fought in March 933, probably near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unstrut">Unstrut</a> river in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thuringia">Thuringia</a>, between King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-the-fowler">Henry the Fowler</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-francia">East Francia</a> and a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magyars">Magyar</a> raiding army. Henry had used a nine-year truce to build fortifications and train armoured cavalry, and when he refused further tribute the Magyars invaded and were routed. The victory raised the prestige of the Saxon dynasty, although Magyar raids continued until Otto I's victory at the Lechfeld in 955.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-riade.jpg" alt="Battle of Riade" width="320" height="203" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Heinrich_I._k%C3%A4mpft_gegen_die_Ungarn.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
